# From biological images to an exact feature table

The introduction to [Applied Machine Learning for Tabular Data](https://aml4td.org/chapters/introduction.html) uses four cells to explain how image data become one-row-per-cell tabular predictors. This lesson preserves that example exactly: the two source images and all values from the published table.

## The source images

The first fluorescence image shows four cells, with cytoskeleton in blue and DNA in red.

![Exact AML4TD four-cell fluorescence image](figures/source/cells.png)

The second source image overlays the detected cell and nucleus boundaries.

![Exact AML4TD segmented-cell image](figures/source/segmented.png)

Both files are byte-for-byte copies of the canonical source assets.

## The exact published table

Each image-derived object becomes one observation. The source's identifiers and six measurements are retained without interpolation or invented values.

```biolang
let cells = read_csv("data/cells.csv")
cells
```

The areas describe cell and nucleus size, eccentricity describes shape, and intensity summarizes the image signal. These are predictors derived from the images; they are not synthetic observations.

```biolang
table({
    check: ["cell count", "ID 17 nucleus area", "ID 22 cell eccentricity", "mean cell intensity"],
    value: [
        nrow(cells),
        cells |> filter(|row| row.ID == 17) |> col("nucleus_area") |> first(),
        cells |> filter(|row| row.ID == 22) |> col("cell_eccentricity") |> first(),
        mean(cells |> col("cell_intensity"))
    ]
})
```

```biolang
assert nrow(cells) == 4, "four exact source cells"
assert ncol(cells) == 7, "identifier plus six exact features"
assert cells |> col("ID") == [17, 18, 21, 22], "source identifiers"
assert cells |> col("nucleus_area") == [3352, 1777, 1274, 1169], "source nucleus areas"
assert cells |> col("cell_area") == [11699, 4980, 3081, 3933], "source cell areas"
assert abs(mean(cells |> col("cell_intensity")) - 0.203) < 1e-12, "source mean cell intensity"
"Exact images and published table verified."
```
